Expected elements: present

A genuinely dense tool surface in a light theme — Code pane full, mono texture consistent, nothing below 4.8:1 — undermined by a column composition that leaves 46% of the middle column white while the Transaction pane runs past the viewport bottom.

This round: (1) landed — the provenance note sets flush-left in its own full-width row (y 224–363); the DATA section (y≈191–363, 173px) is 17% of the pane's 1013px visible height, down from 39–41%. (3) landed for the one state this fixture exercises. (4) landed — line 32 carries a teal ⊙, line 29 a grey ⊘ — but on 2 of 36 rows. (5) landed; the exit reads "← demo". (2) is not verifiable here: no `COST · TRANSACTIONFEE` row is on screen, `COST · MANA` reads `88000 / 200000 mana (FeeJuice)` in base ten, and the pane is cut at y=1075 mid-JSON.

Call Trace measurement: the tabbed region is y 63–668 (606px); content ends at the "By call order. / Self cost" footer, y≈328. Empty = 340px = 56% of the region, 59% below the tab strip — 13.6 unused 25px rows. The standing observation holds, at the top of its range. But height is not the lever: the Values pane below is also 30% empty (122px of 407px). Width is. The widest frame row leaves a 152px dead band before the opcode column (`main` leaves 382px), while the 381px Transaction pane breaks two 42-char addresses across two lines each and wraps three prose blocks to 6/5/3 lines. ~120–130px moved from the middle column costs the call trace nothing.

Fixes: reweight the column split; raise the executed-line marker above a 2×2px dot.

Rating: 6/10

